  "node_id": "lemma_7",
  "edition": "Newton, Principia, Andrew Motte trans., 1729 (Wikisource); Book I, Section I, Lemma VII; Plate 2, Fig. 1.",
  "caption": "The ultimate ratio of the arc, the chord, and the tangent, any one to any other, is the ratio of equality.",
  "n_steps": 3,
  "steps": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "gloss": "The original arc ACB rising from A, with its chord AB and tangent AD, exactly the figure of the preceding lemma."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "gloss": "The auxiliary blow-up: AB and AD produced to distant b and d, the parallel bd, and a similar arc Acb that stays finite."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "gloss": "By Lemma VI the angle dAb vanishes, so Ab, Ad, and arc Acb coincide and become equal; hence AB, AD, ACB acquire the ratio of equality."
    }
  ],
